            <ArticleTitle>A study of synthetic approaches to 2-acyl DHA lysophosphatidic acid.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>8186-8192</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7ob01771e</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lysophosphatidic acid (LPA) is a chemical mediator with a very simple glycerophospholipid structure. 1-Acyl LPA and 2-acyl LPA are biosynthesized in vivo. Unlike 1-acyl LPA, the biological function of 2-acyl LPA has been hardly elucidated and even organic synthesis of 2-acyl LPA had not been established. We suppressed acyl migration by formation of a salt with a phosphate group in order to synthesize 2-acyl LPA condensed with docosahexaenoic acid.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
